__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
*.skill
.superpowers/
# Local-only strategy/working docs — never published; kept outside docs/ so doc_lint
# (which walks the filesystem, not git) doesn't demand index entries CI can't resolve.
docs-private/

# Job-search runtime data — never commit a real résumé / preferences / digest into this public repo
preferences.md
resumes/
reports/

# The live behavior evals — the driver scripts, the case and seed definitions, the baseline
# numbers, and every run's output. Untracked on 2026-08-10: the results carry machine paths and
# live posting text, and nothing else in here is something a user of the plugin needs to read.
# They still run from the working copy. tests/fixtures/seed-workspace/ is the tracked seed the
# workspace validator's own test reads.
#
# The leading slash anchors this to the repository root. Written bare as `evals/` it also matches
# skills/<skill>/evals/. The 14 files already tracked there stay tracked, because a gitignore rule
# never applies to an indexed path (`git ls-files 'skills/*/evals/*' | wc -l` gives 14), but a NEW
# eval file added under any skill would be silently ignored. scripts/eval_harness.py:26 globs
# skills/*/evals/evals.json off the filesystem, so the harness would pass locally while that file
# never reached a commit. Measured with a probe:
# `git check-ignore -v skills/job-search/evals/__probe.json` matched the bare rule and does not
# match the anchored one.
/evals/
